{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120564","id":3916603483,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7pcqBb","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120564","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120564.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120564.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120564","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120564/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120564/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120564/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2d6cc9ae2cb89a0bd5b8ef49fae2fe2395ee3a72","number":120564,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Replace `{project}` with `-r` in VS Code","user":{"login":"Muller-Castro","id":37383316,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzgzMzE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37383316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro","html_url":"https://github.com/Muller-Castro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muller-Castro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nPrevents session overwriting\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n\r\nIf I forget to open the project workspace and click on a script inside Godot, my last VS Code session is not restored.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n- Follow this [tutorial](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/editor/external_editor.html)\r\n- Open the project workspace in VS Code\r\n- Open a few files so they are saved in the session history\r\n- Close the window\r\n- Open Godot and open a script\r\n\r\nThis bypasses the restore behavior, causing all history from the last session to be lost.\r\n\r\nReplacing `{project}` with `--reuse-window` eliminates the risk of losing the session:\r\n- If no VS Code window is open: The script opens in a new window without a workspace\r\n- If the window with the project workspace is already open: It will be reused\r\n- If the project workspace window is not open, but another VS Code window is: That open window will be used instead\r\n\r\nI'm using the [flatpak](https://github.com/flathub/org.godotengine.Godot) version of Godot with these editor settings:\r\n- **Exec Path:** `flatpak-spawn`\r\n- **Exec Flags:** `--host code --reuse-window --goto {file}:{line}:{col}`","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzM